<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/10th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Fýrisvellir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 985</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Battle of the Fyris Wolds</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Fýrisvellir was fought in the 980s on the plains near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppsala">Uppsala</a>, where King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-the-victorious">Eric the Victorious</a> of the Swedes defeated his nephew Styrbjörn the Strong, who had come with a Danish and Jomsviking force. It is known mainly from Norse sagas and skaldic poetry, with possible echoes on runestones. The victory secured Eric's rule and gave him his byname.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-fyrisvellir.jpg" alt="Battle of Fýrisvellir" width="320" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mårten Eskil Winge · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Efter_slaget_vid_Fyrisvall.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
